  "epistemic_status": "hypothesized",
  "title": "Observer physics is a projection of object self-knowledge",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "a167d57d-da69-4c4d-9b8f-311e12a88dcd",
      "text": "Every term of physics names an observer measuring something an object does. The conjecture is that each such term is the image under a projection $\\Pi$ of an operator the object has from inside, so laws are what objects' self-operations look like from outside.",
